ChatSched — Claude fixes, Sept 7
=================================

Scope: this file documents ONLY the seventh task resolved from
"Claude To fix 1..txt" — item 11, HIGH: Launch-credit race condition.
Items 5 through 10 were already completed and documented separately
("claude fixes Sept 1" through "Sept 6"). Items 12 and 13 were left
untouched.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What the finding said, verified against the real source
------------------------------------------------------------------------
supabase/functions/payfast-checkout/index.ts read
business_launch_credits.remaining, computed creditApplied in JavaScript,
wrote payment state, and — for a partially-covered payment — deferred the
ACTUAL business_launch_credits.remaining deduction to a later,
completely separate request: payfast-notify's redeemLaunchCredit(), which
only runs once PayFast's webhook confirms the payment. Two concurrent
checkouts for two different payments belonging to the same business could
each read the same pre-deduction "remaining" figure before either one's
write took effect.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. A design principle I found and preserved, not just a bug to squash
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Before changing anything, I found that the deferred-deduction design
wasn't accidental — schema_phase55_subscriptions.sql's own comment on
payments.credit_applied says the deduction is deliberately deferred
"until payfast-notify confirms the payment actually completed, the same
way payments.status itself only ever changes from that webhook, never
from checkout." That's a real, sensible principle: don't spend a
business's credit on a payment that might never actually go through.

But I also found the race is real in BOTH branches of payfast-checkout,
not just the partial-coverage one the finding's own phrasing most
directly describes:
  - For a FULLY-covered campaign (credit >= amount), the code marks the
    payment 'paid' immediately, with no PayFast round-trip and no later
    confirmation step at all. This branch has no opportunity to defer
    anything — its "reservation" and its "confirmation" are the same
    atomic moment, so the deferred-deduction principle doesn't apply to
    it, and it needed an immediate, atomic fix regardless.
  - For the partially-covered branch, the deferred-deduction principle is
    worth keeping, but the COMPUTATION that decides how much credit a
    given payment gets to claim still has to be race-free the instant
    it's decided — otherwise two concurrent checkouts could each
    provisionally claim the full remaining balance before either
    outcome is known.

This is why the fix is a reserve -> confirm/release pattern, not a
single "deduct everything at checkout" change: it closes the race for
both branches while keeping the original "don't finalize until PayFast
confirms" principle intact for the branch where it still applies.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. The fix
------------------------------------------------------------------------
supabase/schema_phase88_atomic_launch_credit_redemption.sql (NEW):
  - launch_credit_redemptions — one row per payment that ever claimed
    credit. UNIQUE(payment_id) is both the payment-to-credit relation and
    the idempotency key the finding asks for: a payment can only ever
    have one redemption row, so a retried reserve call detects "already
    reserved" and returns the existing figures instead of reserving
    again. status: reserved -> confirmed (payment completed, no further
    balance change) or released (payment failed/cancelled, amount added
    back).
  - reserve_launch_credit_for_payment(payment_id) — called from
    payfast-checkout at checkout time. Locks the business's one
    business_launch_credits row (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) for the duration
    of the transaction — this is the actual fix: two concurrent calls for
    the same business now serialize on this lock, so the second one
    always sees the balance the first one actually left, never a stale
    pre-deduction value. Computes and immediately deducts
    LEAST(remaining, payment.amount), inserts the redemption row, updates
    payments.credit_applied.
  - confirm_launch_credit_redemption(payment_id) — called from
    payfast-notify on COMPLETE. No balance math — the deduction already
    happened at reservation time — just flips the redemption to
    'confirmed' so it can never be released later.
  - release_launch_credit_redemption(payment_id) — called from
    payfast-notify on FAILED or CANCELLED. Locks the same credit row and
    adds the reserved amount back to remaining, then marks the redemption
    'released'. A no-op if nothing was reserved, or if the redemption is
    already confirmed/released — safe to call unconditionally.
  - All three: PUBLIC execute revoked, granted only to authenticated —
    same defense-in-depth convention established in item 7.

supabase/functions/payfast-checkout/index.ts (EDITED):
  - Replaced the read-compute-write sequence with a single call to
    reserve_launch_credit_for_payment(). For the fully-covered branch,
    also calls confirm_launch_credit_redemption() in the same request
    right after marking the payment paid — there's no later webhook to
    defer to for this branch, so its reservation is confirmed
    immediately rather than left 'reserved' forever.
  - Removed the now-unused local applyLaunchCredit() helper.

supabase/functions/payfast-notify/index.ts (EDITED):
  - The COMPLETE branch now calls confirm_launch_credit_redemption()
    instead of the old redeemLaunchCredit() (deleted — its only caller
    was this line, confirmed via grep before removal).
  - Added a CANCELLED branch (previously only FAILED was handled) —
    both now mark the payment failed and call
    release_launch_credit_redemption(), so credit isn't left stuck
    reserved against a payment that will never complete.
  - Fixed a second, real, separate bug found while making this change:
    the amount-mismatch check compared PayFast's actual charge against
    the FULL payment.amount, even though payfast-checkout only ever asks
    PayFast to charge amountDue (the post-credit figure). This meant any
    partially-credit-covered payment would ALWAYS fail this check and
    could never actually be marked paid — broken before this redesign
    touched anything, found because the redesign needed a correct
    "expected" figure to confirm against. Now compares against
    payment.amount - payment.credit_applied.

supabase/tests/atomic_launch_credit_redemption_test.sql (NEW):
  - pgTAP test file, 12 assertions. A true race between concurrent
    requests can't be simulated inside one pgTAP transaction (there's
    only one session) — what it proves instead is that the sequential
    state transitions serialize correctly: a R60 payment against a R100
    balance is fully covered; a second R60 payment for the same business
    then only gets the genuinely-remaining R40, not a stale R100;
    re-reserving the first payment again returns the stored figure
    rather than attempting a fresh, impossible deduction; confirming one
    reservation and releasing a different one only affects the released
    payment's own amount; and releasing an already-confirmed redemption
    is a safe no-op that doesn't give back money already spent.

supabase/DEPLOY.md (EDITED): new section covering both fixes, redeploy
steps for the two changed functions, and the known gap below.

